This assumes `InvoiceService.create` returns `InvoiceDtos.InvoiceResponse`. If it returns another record, map it to `InvoiceResponse` in the controller, or change the return type.

Conventions applied: the DTOs are records in an `InvoiceDtos` holder, with `jakarta.validation` on the request. The controller uses constructor injection, has no try/catch, and wraps the result in `ApiResponse.ok`.

The request fields are boxed `Long` so a missing value fails `@NotNull` instead of silently becoming 0. `note` is optional, so it only has `@Size(max = 200)`. The endpoint returns 201 Created.

